<SiteLayout title="About" description="HaloForge Labs builds Halowin Bubo, an open-source native Windows LLM server for AMD Strix Halo laptops.">
  <span class="eyebrow">HaloForge Labs</span>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="intro">HaloForge Labs presents Halowin Bubo and its documentation. Bubo is an open-source, native Windows LLM server for AMD Strix Halo laptops.</p>
  <div class="article-grid">
    <section class="article-body"><h2>Built on gufo</h2><p>Bubo is a fork of <a href="https://github.com/gufo-org/gufo">gufo</a>, the open-source LLM server. The gufo authors provide the upstream server. gufo uses the MIT license.</p><h2>The name</h2><p>Halowin joins Halo, from Strix Halo, and Windows. Bubo is a genus of owl, and “gufo” is Italian for owl. The owl mark is the Egyptian hieroglyph for owl (G17), drawn from the Noto Sans Egyptian Hieroglyphs font under the SIL Open Font License.</p><p><a href="/bubo/">Read about Halowin Bubo</a> or <a href="/docs/">open the documentation</a>.</p></section>
    <aside class="margin-note"><span class="eyebrow">Source and support</span><p><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo">Source code</a><br /><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/issues">Report an issue</a><br /><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/releases">Releases</a></p></aside>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
